our to see architectural and collection highlights. Book before the weekend because capacity is limited.","short_summary":"A structured way to see the library’s public highlights.","evidence_claim":"NYPL offers free one-hour docent-led building tours at 11 AM and 2 PM Monday through Saturday, with online tickets released weekly.","source_url":"https://www.nypl.org/events/tours/schwarzman","source_title":"Stephen A. Schwarzman Building Tours","source_kind":"cultural_institution","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Free tours require online reservation and have limited capacity; verify current times and ticket release details.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"grand-central-terminal","subject_type":"place","entity_name":"Grand Central Terminal","title":"Continue to Grand Central Terminal","subtitle":"89 East 42nd Street","notes":"Walk east along 42nd Street to the terminal and enter the Main Concourse. Take a moment to identify the information booth clock and the ceiling before exploring further.","short_summary":"A historic transit landmark within the same Midtown walk.","evidence_claim":"Grand Central Terminal’s official visitor page lists its address as 89 East 42nd Street and identifies the terminal as open to the public daily.","source_url":"https://mobile.grandcentralterminal.com/visit/","source_title":"Visit Grand Central Terminal","source_kind":"business_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"The terminal is currently listed as open daily 5:15 AM–2:00 AM; individual tenants keep separate hours.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"grand-central-whispering-gallery","subject_type":"place","entity_name":"Whispering Gallery at Grand Central Terminal","title":"Find the Whispering Gallery","subtitle":"Grand Central Terminal, near the Oyster Bar","notes":"Pair up and try the gallery’s corner-to-corner acoustics without blocking foot traffic. Keep your voices low and treat it as a quick architectural detail, not a performance.","short_summary":"A small, memorable acoustic feature inside the terminal.","evidence_claim":"Grand Central Terminal’s official “What to See” page directs visitors to lean into opposite corners of the gallery to hear each other across the room.","source_url":"https://grandcentralterminal.com/what-to-see/","source_title":"What to See at Grand Central Terminal","source_kind":"business_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Keep clear of commuter paths and follow any on-site directions from terminal staff.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true}],"warnings":[]}],"warnings":[]}
